      "content": "Assessing the \"merit\" of specific conspiracy claims is difficult because most details lack verifiable evidence or logical consistency when scrutinized. While some political and social frustration is real and can be shaped by legitimate policy disagreements, the dramatic narratives of a secretly rigged system often rely on exaggeration or misinterpretation of data to provoke strong reactions.\n\nIn a way, these claims act as a \"perception of control\" mechanism that explains away the complexity of modern power dynamics in a simple, emotionally satisfying way, even if the factual underpinnings are flawed. The truth likely lies in the middle: there are genuine institutional flaws and information asymmetries, but the movement usually amplifies these into total systematic conspiracy rather than nuanced critique.",
